    "scope": "Two actually inspected whole northern/eastern and western photographs,standard viewer PMTiles/DEM only.No bespoke plans/surveys.Reference photos viewed only,not redistributed or used as texture maps.",
    "pictures": [
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:St_Elisabeth_Cathedral_Kosice.jpeg",
        "author": "Ingo Mehling",
        "date": "2019-06-09 (file summary; EXIF2019-06-08)",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-3.0 or GFDL1.2+",
        "observed": "Actually inspected whole northern/eastern oblique. Pale/varied stone Gothic cruciform body,polygonal choir,low aisle/chapel perimeter,stepped buttresses/pinnacles and pierced parapets. Red/ochre/slate diamond/zigzag roof pattern,slender central metal fleche. North clock tower has tall staged pointed windows and dark onion crown with gold ribs/clock faces/open upper lantern. Major transept has tall pointed glazing,ornamental triangular gable and deeply recessed portal. Upper side bays include blind tracery;fine sculpture/roof motif sequence approximated."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_of_St._Elizabeth%27s_Cathedral_from_Alzbetina_street.jpg",
        "author": "Lacpo",
        "date": "2020-01-08",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-4.0",
        "observed": "Actually inspected western whole view along Alzbetina street. Unequal west towers: tall northern onion/clock tower at left; lower southern tower at right has a dark pyramidal cap. Central west facade has a tall pointed window,deep portal and ornate triangular tracery gable with small pinnacles. Central metal fleche rises behind the gable. Street buildings occlude outer lower aisles;fine sculpture,inscriptions and exact clock decorations are not copied."
      }
    ]
